  "result": "Perfect! All 84 tests pass. I've successfully added line discounts with the following implementation:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/errors.js** \u2014 Added DISCOUNT_INVALID error code\n\n2. **src/invoices.js** \u2014 Updated functions to support discounts:\n   - Added `isValidDiscount()` helper to validate discount percentage (0-100, can be decimal)\n   - **createInvoice()** \u2014 Accepts optional `discountPercent` per line, defaults to 0, validates it\n   - **addLine()** \u2014 Accepts optional `discountPercent`, validates it, stores on new line\n   - **invoiceTotals()** \u2014 Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, total }`:\n     - subtotal = sum of line totals\n     - discount = sum of (lineTotal \u00d7 discountPercent \u00f7 100), rounded per line\n     - total = subtotal - discount, clamped to 0 minimum\n   - **removeLine()** and **issueInvoice()** \u2014 Updated to work with new line structure\n\n3. **Tests** \u2014 Comprehensive coverage:\n   - Discount validation (0-100, decimals like 12.5, non-numeric, out of range)\n   - Discount calculations (10%, 12.5%, 20%, 60%, 100%)\n   - Multiple lines with different discounts\n   - Total clamping to 0 for 100% discount\n   - addLine with discounts\n\nKey features:\n- Decimal discounts supported (12.5% is valid)\n- All amounts computed with `roundCents()`\n- Total never goes below 0 (clamped with `Math.max()`)\n- Input immutability maintained throughout",
